Myriad's TypeScript implementation follows upstream revision
d48825867acd081de22b0e7b5585bb562288796d. The original JavaScript and HTML
were used only to calibrate the migration and are not retained or executed by
the product or its tests. Standalone module tests now cover public behavior,
edge cases, and fixed multi-frame regression fingerprints.

Import correctness fixes were selectively ported from revision
8deb51b7f93984191dfd5805becb349bbe58f90f (2026-09-07): semantic alpha unions,
per-side close-diff synthesis, empty-layer handling, narrow-strand spacing,
and alpha-aware resampling/compositing. Its prepass eye-mask approach informs
Myriad's independent left-eye, right-eye and collar stencil bits. This does not
update the pinned reference runtime or adopt the demo's alternate-blink policy.
The same update informs Worker-owned PSD preflight/decoding and iris reopening
squash/rebound. Myriad retains its stricter import limits and compiler; the
rebound is a smaller, endpoint-windowed variation on the existing blink clock.

The generic close-diff RGBA data and decoder are ported in
../upstream/genericParts.ts; tests pin the decoded pixels by SHA-256. The base
bind, deform, and fade math follows the upstream runtime. Myriad supplies its
own bounded ambient and text-free preview speech timing.

The surrounding Myriad page, overlay, and settings chrome are not from that project.

Ellipsoid head/scalp projection, side-profile shaping, feathered hairline-pin,
delayed topwear/bottomwear cylinder projection, and bounded chest-volume yaw
and silhouette response were adapted from the MIT-licensed research fork at
https://github.com/izumix77/Anime2.5DRig, revision
1644759cd451ab82065e2bf57b21fe806e2be334. Myriad reimplements those behaviors
inside its versioned asset contract and bounded motion runtime; the fork's demo
UI, breast-curve editor and manual silhouette tuning, localStorage tuning,
camera input, and recording paths are not included. The chest curve, near/far
response, and breathing behavior are represented as a single bounded field
derived from Myriad's existing garment-support profile rather than copied as
manual per-model controls.
